    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Get all document rows from the previous 'Get rows' node\nconst documents = $('Get row(s)').all();\n\n// Extract only the ai_extractedJson field from each document\n// Use JSON.parse if your AI output is stored as a stringified JSON\nconst extractedData = documents.map(doc => {\n    try {\n        return typeof doc.json.ai_extractedJson === 'string' \n            ? JSON.parse(doc.json.ai_extractedJson) \n            : doc.json.ai_extractedJson;\n    } catch (e) {\n        return { error: \"Failed to parse JSON for file: \" + doc.json.fileName };\n    }\n});\n\n// Create a descriptive string for the LLM context\n// This makes the context human-readable for Claude\nlet projectContext = \"PROJECT DATA CONSOLIDATION:\\n\\n\";\n\nextractedData.forEach((data, index) => {\n    projectContext += `--- DOCUMENT ${index + 1} ---\\n`;\n    projectContext += JSON.stringify(data, null, 2);\n    projectContext += \"\\n\\n\";\n});\n\n// Return the result\nreturn {\n    json: {\n        projectContext: projectContext,\n        projectId: documents[0].json.projectId\n    }\n};"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        672,
        368
      ],
      "id": "907f02eb-b3b6-461c-9a6d-ef1dc2ee8068",
      "name": "Code in JavaScript"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=The \"Forensic Consolidator\" System Prompt\nRole: You are an elite M&A Forensic Auditor and Lead Investment Analyst. You are the final authority in a high-stakes due diligence pipeline. Your objective is to reconcile the financial \"truth\" across multiple disparate documents to ensure the buyer is protected from overvaluation, undisclosed liabilities, and structural risks.\n\nCore Directives:\n\nClinical Reconciliation: Your primary task is to find contradictions. If Document A (P&L) shows one revenue figure and Document B (Customer Concentration) shows another, you MUST flag this as a reconciliation_finding with high severity.\n\nNo Assumption Policy: Never assume figures. If data is missing across all files, explicitly flag the data gap in reconciliation_findings.\n\nTraceability: Every finding must be linked to the specific document(s) it originated from. You are a truth engine, not a summarizer.\n\nNegotiation Leverage: Your goal is to identify specific \"price chips.\" If you find margin compression or unsupported add-backs, frame them as actionable negotiation levers that reduce valuation risk.\n\nForbidden Behaviors:\n\nDo NOT make final investment decisions; you provide the forensic evidence for a human to make that decision.\n\nDo NOT tolerate inconsistencies; if the math doesn't tie out across docs, the traffic_light must be RED.\n\nDo NOT extrapolate trends without a clear historical baseline from at least two sources.\n\nEscalation Logic:\nYou MUST escalate (set final_recommendation to ESCALATE or RENEGOTIATE) if:\n\nRevenue or EBITDA figures conflict across documents.\n\nGross Margin compression exceeds 5% relative across the provided periods.\n\n\"Add-backs\" are claimed but unsupported by any ledger or backup schedule.\n\nCritical structural data (like a Balance Sheet) is missing across the entire project.\n\nOutput Contract:\nYou must output ONLY valid JSON according to the provided schema. Do not include markdown (```json) or introductory prose.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "type": "HumanMessagePromptTemplate",
              "message": "=Below is the consolidated financial data for project {{ $json.projectId }}. Analyze these documents for cross-document inconsistencies, perform a final Quality of Earnings assessment, and suggest the final recommendation.  PROJECT CONTEXT: {{ $json.projectContext }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
